 "approvalMessage": {
  "approvalNumber": 3,
  "billId": {
   "basePrintNo": "A2655",
   "basePrintNoStr": "A2655-2019",
   "printNo": "A2655",
   "session": 2019,
   "version": ""
  },
  "chapter": 133,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 3 Chapter 133\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2655, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\n        the uniform treatment of waste\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  I am pleased to sign  this  legislation,  which  amends  Environmental\nConservation Law (ECL) Section 27-0903 to require that all waste related\nto  the  exploration and production of oil and natural gas be considered\nhazardous waste if such waste meets the existing definition of hazardous\nwaste provided in ECL Section 27-0901. The Commissioner of  the  Depart-\nment  of  Environmental Conservation is required pursuant to ECL Section\n27-0903 to promulgate a list of hazardous wastes identified  by  charac-\nteristic,  which is laid out in very detailed regulations promulgated by\nthe subject matter experts at the DEC.\n \n  This bill recognizes that wastes from the development and operation of\noil and natural gas wells may qualify as hazardous under DEC's  existing\nhazardous  waste  regulations  at  6 NYCRR Part 371. Hazardous waste has\nsignificantly more stringent handling and tracking  requirements,  which\nis  important  given  the significant impact that such waste can have on\nhuman and environmental health.\n \n  However, it is important to clarify  that  this  bill  identifies  the\nwaste  streams  that should be subject to the hazardous waste program as\nopposed to the solid waste management program, but  the  bill  does  not\nreplace  or  usurp  DEC's discretion to apply its technical expertise in\ndetermining how each waste stream associated with oil  and  natural  gas\nproduction  should  be managed. I am signing this bill on that basis, so\nthat DEC can continue to protect the health of all New Yorkers, and this\nbill builds on that robust statutory and regulatory framework.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2020
 },
